{"lines": ["USS Cyclops was a huge Navy coal ship, and in March 1918 she left Barbados for Baltimore.", "A cylinder in her starboard engine was cracked, and she was carrying about 10,800 tons of manganese ore, far over her limit.", "At Barbados, the water was already over her load line.", "Her captain, George Worley, had been born in Germany under another name.", "Former crew later said he cursed his men, and once chased an officer around the ship with a pistol.", "They said he walked his rounds in long underwear and a derby hat.", "Then the Cyclops sailed north, and was never seen again.", "No wreckage, and no bodies, ever.", "The Navy's own investigation said, \"Many theories have been advanced, but none that satisfactorily accounts for her disappearance.\"", "And two of her sister ships, Proteus and Nereus, later vanished at sea too.", "So far, everything vanished, but the strangest cases are the ones where something was left behind."], "words": [["USS", 0.0, 0.32], ["Cyclops", 0.32, 1.08], ["was", 1.08, 1.22], ["a", 1.22, 1.34], ["huge", 1.34, 1.62], ["Navy", 1.62, 2.0], ["coal", 2.0, 2.38], ["ship,", 2.38, 2.74], ["and", 3.28, 3.36], ["in", 3.36, 3.46], ["March", 3.46, 3.66], ["1918", 3.66, 4.62], ["she", 4.62, 6.08], ["left", 6.08, 6.28], ["Barbados", 6.28, 6.88], ["for", 6.88, 7.2], ["Baltimore.", 7.2, 7.44], ["A", 8.1, 8.24], ["cylinder", 8.24, 8.54], ["in", 8.54, 8.88], ["her", 8.88, 8.98], ["starboard", 8.98, 9.4], ["engine", 9.4, 9.72], ["was", 9.72, 10.02], ["cracked,", 10.02, 10.38], ["and", 10.98, 11.04], ["she", 11.04, 11.14], ["was", 11.14, 11.24], ["carrying", 11.24, 11.58], ["about", 11.58, 11.9], ["10,800", 11.9, 13.1], ["tons", 13.1, 13.64], ["of", 13.64, 13.98], ["manganese", 13.98, 14.56], ["ore,", 14.56, 14.8], ["far", 14.8, 15.5], ["over", 15.5, 15.92], ["her", 15.92, 16.16], ["limit.", 16.16, 16.4], ["At", 16.86, 17.04], ["Barbados,", 17.04, 17.64], ["the", 18.08, 18.22], ["water", 18.22, 18.48], ["was", 18.48, 18.8], ["already", 18.8, 19.14